-- US-3125: seventeen snow, surf, bike and moto brands.
--
-- Catalogues read 2026-09-07 with scripts/ops/shopify-brand-harvest.mjs. Same
-- rules as 00734 and 00739: a colour on five or more products, a brand with at
-- least eight such colours and no more than 35% plain colour words, base_color
-- and shade from the brand's own facet where it publishes one and
-- aspect-normalize's family table otherwise.
--
-- Howler Brothers also returned a feed and is NOT here -- the KB has it already.
--
-- -- REGISTERED NUMBERS: SIX BRANDS, NINE NUMBERS ----------------------------
--
--     Armada             RN 128660   ARMADA SKIS, INC.                [ALPINE SKIS OUTERWEAR]
--     Dakine             RN 91245    DAKINE, INC.                     [LUGGAGE OUTERWEAR BAGS GLOVES]
--     Dakine             RN 163341   Dakine                           [Men's and Women's apparel]
--     Jetty              RN 115296   JETTY LIFE LLC                   [T-SHIRTS]
--     Jetty              RN 158050   Jetty Life, LLC                  [Baby Children's Men's Women's]
--     Picture Organic    RN 153791   Picture Organic Clothing Corp
--     Seager             RN 167606   Seager Inc.                      [Men's apparel]
--     Troy Lee Designs   RN 134405   TROY LEE DESIGNS                 [MOTORCYCLE RACING APPARAL]
--
-- Dakine and Jetty each hold TWO exact-name registrations, and both are kept.
-- This is not the Primitive ambiguity from 00747, where two different companies
-- both fit -- here the pairs are one company registered twice, decades apart
-- (Dakine at 91245 near Stussy's 94974, then again at 163341), which is what
-- the 00750 sequence predicts for a 1979 brand that re-registered. A garment
-- can carry either number, so the KB has to hold both.
--
-- Picture Organic Clothing Corp's product line reads "Towels / Washcloths /
-- Dishcloths" for a ski and snowboard brand. Recorded as seen: the name is
-- exact and the registrant is plainly the company.
--
-- -- ELEVEN REFUSED, THREE OF THEM A NEW SHAPE -------------------------------
--
-- Almond Surfboards, Carve Designs, Salty Crew, Smith Optics and WeatherWool
-- return NOTHING. A legitimate absence.
--
-- Orage is the substring trap, sixteen: OR-AGE-N WEAR LLC, plus FACT-ORAGE,
-- ANCH-ORAGE FURS and A.C. BANG ANCH-ORAGE.
--
-- Club Ride (CLUB APPAREL, LLC, product line BICYCLE CLOTHING) and Mountain
-- Khakis (MK Acquisition LLC, product line PANTS) each return a registrant whose
-- product line is exactly right and whose name drops or abbreviates the label's
-- distinctive token. Same answer as Billabong in 00747.
--
-- The new shape is the FOUNDER REGISTRATION, and it needs separating from the
-- Ulla Johnson acceptance in 00749:
--
--     SHREDLY   ->  ASHLEY RANKIN     [WOMEN'S ACTIVEWEAR]
--     Coal      ->  BRAD SCHEUFFELE   [KNIT HATS WOVEN HATS]
--     Birdwell  ->  HEATHER DENISE BIRDWELL   [CLOTHING]
--
-- All three are a natural person registering for exactly the goods the brand
-- makes, and all three are refused. Ulla Johnson was accepted because THE LABEL
-- IS THE PERSON'S NAME, so the registrant and the brand share every distinctive
-- token. Ashley Rankin does not appear in "SHREDLY" and Brad Scheuffele does not
-- appear in "Coal". Birdwell is the closest -- the surname IS the label -- but
-- Birdwell Beach Britches was founded by Carrie Birdwell Mann, and a different
-- Birdwell registering for generic "CLOTHING" is a namesake until something says
-- otherwise. A founder's own registration is only usable when the founder's
-- name is the brand's name.
--
-- -- COLOURS ----------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- Seeded: almondsurf (9), armada (10), carvedesigns (177), dakine (223), orage (20), pictureorganic (145), shredly (20), smithoptics (135), troyleedesigns (103), weatherwool (8).
-- Palette refused, too few or too plain: birdwell (22, 41% plain), clubride (4), coalheadwear (19, 42% plain), jetty (58, 47% plain).
-- No colour survives the filter: mountainkhakis (0 raw), saltycrew (3 raw), seager (0 raw).
--
